I've taken out plenty of priests with thrown daggers, arrows, crossbow
bolts and rocks.  I do it by cutting out the wall and firing from
outside.  That why the lightning bolt never hits and the deity does not
try switching to disintegration.  When dancing around the 3 squares the
main risk is having the priest start generating insects too soon. 
Already being expert at dagger and doing multifire tends to kill the
priest faster, but I have lucked out and killed the priest completely
with single thrown rocks before any insects are generated.

If you do boulders to force the priest into a single line that reduces
the dancing and thus reduces the time the priest has to generate
insects.  Okay plan especially if dwarves or hulks have trashed the
level leaving enough boulders behind.

If you are using boulders other have reported that it is possible to use
them to dance the priest into a corner.  Then anger the priest and use
the unlimited insects in a sacrifest to get unlimited spell books and AC
points or a paryer fest going for artifact gifts.  Probably a better use
of the boulders - But I tend to value the priest's robe so much I want
it more than I want the endless sacrifest.  The problem with the
sarcifest using insects is you have to leave the priest alive in the end
unless a digger clears the way for your ever stronger pet to kill the
priest for you.

> OTOH, there's this handy c-corpse that I've got, and I'd like to take
